    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIAs">III As</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q">Septimum: ut omnis homo teneat homines suos in fideiussione sua contra omne furtum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#attenborough" n="7" corresp="#wit-q">Septimum, ut omnis homo teneat homines suos in fideiussione sua contra omne furtum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-q">Seventhly, every man shall stand surety for his own men against every [charge of] crime.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIIEm_7">III Em 7</ref>; <ref target="clause:IAtr_1-1_dup2">I Atr 1.10</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Latin only; no German translation in Liebermann.</note>
      </div>
